WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:08.660
. In the immediate, there is no better time
than now to talk a little bit about the plans

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:15.679
for people who are voting in very blue states
and in very red states who maybe are planning

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:17.610
to vote third party.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:22.650
Maybe you're planning not to vote at all because
the outcome in your state is essentially determined.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.600
Now, as most of you probably know, in the
United States, we don't have a national popular

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.600
vote.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.600
We have an electoral college.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:35.219
So if you win a state as a presidential candidate
by just one vote, you get all of that state's

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.589
electoral votes and it has no impact on what
happens in other states.

00:00:39.589 --> 00:00:46.059
It's really 50 individual elections because
of that system that we have really.

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:50.690
The election is determined by a dozen or so
battleground states or swing states, as they're

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.859
sometimes called.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:58.850
So these include places like Wisconsin, North
Carolina, Ohio, Florida, etc.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.440
And it's very common that people in very blue
are very red.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.650
States who are on the left will say to me,
I get these phone calls.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.790
I hear from people in person, et cetera.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.329
They'll say, you know, I live in Utah.

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:11.630
Biden's not going to win.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.630
I might vote third party or I might not vote
or whatever.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.130
And then I'll hear from people in states like
my state of Massachusetts who say Biden is

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:21.289
winning by what is it at this point, 34.

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:23.240
It's crazy what Biden is winning by.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:28.929
In Massachusetts, it doesn't really require
my vote to make sure Biden gets Massachusetts

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:29.929
electoral votes.

00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:31.929
So I might vote.

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:35.520
Maybe I'll vote Green Party to give them some
support or whatever.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.750
If there was ever an election where that is
not the approach that we should have, it is

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.799
this one.

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:47.259
If there was ever an election where every
blue state and red state voter needs to make

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:50.399
sure that you are voting for Joe Biden, it
is this one.

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:54.079
And you probably can guess why I'm going to
make this point.

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:59.840
There is a very real possibility that Donald
Trump will claim that the election wasn't

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.600
fair, that it was rigged, that the results
are wrong.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:10.420
And in particular, if it's very close nationally
or within the key states that end up being

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.500
the determining factors.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.340
We may have a situation where not only do
we not know the results on November 3rd, I

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.410
mean, with the number of mail in ballots we're
going to have, it's certainly reasonable and

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:24.659
not a problem for me that maybe we don't know
the results until November 6th or 7th, 7th.

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:27.470
I want the right results rather than the fast
results.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.629
But put that aside for a second.

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:33.540
We could again end up with a situation where
the Supreme Court gets involved here.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.050
And some people sent me a clip of Sam Ceder
recently talking about this, saying we might

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.659
not know who won on Tuesday.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:45.180
And Trump will in all likelihood claim that
he won.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.730
Lawsuits may start in a variety of different
states and it could be a never ending battle.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:55.260
So we need a large margin in every single
state.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.489
And also we want the largest possible popular
vote margin.

00:02:58.489 --> 00:02:59.489
Why?

00:02:59.489 --> 00:03:06.459
Well, because if it does get to either secretaries
of state or Supreme Court justices, the more

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:09.739
overwhelming the defeat is of Donald Trump.

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:14.069
If we are going to get one, the more difficult
that's going to be for Supreme Court justices

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:16.290
to justify funny business.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.709
We'll leave it at that which could end up
handing the election to Donald Trump.

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:21.550
There's no guarantee.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.270
As we know, the Supreme Court is liable to
do anything at any time.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:30.060
But the point is winning the popular vote
by three million votes, which is roughly what

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.870
Hillary Clinton did in 2016 while still seeing
Donald Trump become president with an Electoral

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.370
College victory.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.880
That's just going to be too close.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.409
And if this extends a few days into weeks
because of lawsuits and on and on into the

00:03:43.409 --> 00:03:48.659
Supreme Court, particularly while Donald Trump
is trying to kneecap the Postal Service to

00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:53.750
try to prevent a vote by mail, absentee ballots
from being delivered, we need to do everything

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.330
we can to avoid small margins anywhere.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:01.310
We want to avoid small margins in the states
that will be close.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:06.000
We want to avoid small margins or smaller
margins than we could have in California and

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.000
Massachusetts.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.090
We need to run the score up.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:13.290
And if the election comes down to a couple
of states and the popular vote is closer rather

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:19.140
than less close, it just better enables Donald
Trump to claim whatever the hell he plans

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.140
to claim.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:25.690
If we overwhelm the vote so much that Trump
is crushed in the popular vote, the claims

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:28.360
are just slightly harder to make seriously.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.580
California has millions and millions of Democrats,
and Joe Biden's clearly going to win.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.580
Who cares?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.210
Go out and vote and run up the score in California.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.210
Massachusetts will.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.200
Easily go to Joe Biden.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.750
You'd better believe I'm going to be voting
and encouraging everybody I know who votes

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.730
in Massachusetts to be voting.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.110
Everybody has to vote because we have to.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:51.160
I don't know of a better term than to run
up the score.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:57.660
And then and only then, if we succeed in removing
Donald Trump, then we go back to what I discussed

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:05.580
earlier, which is we will have to deal with
Trump ism and the 60, 62, 64, 66 million people

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.970
who will have seen the last three and a half
years and will say, yeah, give me another

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.990
four years of that following.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:15.030
Sam Cedar's logic on this, which I think is
sound.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:21.590
It's possible that overwhelming margins could
sway one Supreme Court justice.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:27.100
You don't have to if it's going to be five,
four in some decision over some lawsuit that

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:32.130
Trump files, if it's going to be five for
an overwhelming popular vote.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.500
Big victory swinging.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:38.960
One of those nine votes could make all the
difference in who ends up being president

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.420
as of January 20th, 2021.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.600
And voting is something we can all do.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:45.600
It's our right.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.680
Let's exercise it.

